## Topics

`team /` first hires by stage, roles and ownership maps, compensation and incentives,
onboarding, founder time allocation, when to stop doing it yourself, hiring process
for a small brand.
`sops /` SOP writing and structure, documentation that survives staff turnover,
release and approval processes, weekly operating rhythm, project management cadence,
team tooling stack.
`partners /` in-house versus agency versus freelancer, how to brief an agency, how to
hold one accountable, contractor agreements and scope, when to fire an agency, what
to keep in-house permanently.
`fulfilment /` 3PL selection and negotiation, warehouse and pick-pack operations,
carrier selection and rates, shipping SLAs, damage and shrinkage, returns processing
operations, international fulfilment.
`support /` support desk staffing by ticket volume, response time SLAs, macros and
knowledge base, escalation paths, tooling, quality monitoring.

## Look for

Real hire sequences from operators who have done it, with the revenue level attached.
What a 3PL actually costs per order at different volumes, broken out by receiving,
storage, pick, pack and ship. What an SOP needs to contain to survive the person who
wrote it leaving.

## Scope mix

Mostly growth, gated hard on stage and team size. Small baseline: someone owns each
surface by name, a release has an approval step, support has a stated response time,
and the fulfilment partner has a measured error rate.
